From 589477876b4b6108f5fbc72654f5d006d05d5f55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Doze-off <viniciussadxxx@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 14:20:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] bpfloader: add universal legacy-kernel BPF toggle

This adds a runtime-controlled compatibility mode for devices using older
kernels with backported BPF features.

The property is intentionally read from
persist.sys.phh.traffic_indicator_fallback instead of relying on
ro.bpf.kver_override from product.prop.

When the property is true or unset, bpfloader uses the real kernel version
reported by uname().

When the property is false, bpfloader reports kernel version 5.10.239
to enable BPF feature gates required by the firewall-bypass compatibility
path.

This patch is universal and is not tied to a specific processor or SoC
vendor. It can be used on supported Qualcomm, MediaTek, Samsung Exynos,
Unisoc, and other devices.

- Warning: disabling the fallback may break the traffic
- indicator and can cause a black screen, OEM screen, boot failure, Wi-Fi
- initialization failure, or bootloader screen on devices whose kernels do
- not provide the required BPF backports.

The fallback is enabled by default. If the fallback remains enabled, the
firewall-bypass patch may not work on some devices. On supported MediaTek
kernels, the MTK BPF Patcher app may be required to restore firewall-bypass
compatibility.

The MTK BPF Patcher app is optional and is only intended
for supported MediaTek kernels. It is not required by this universal patch
and must not be used on non-MediaTek devices.

- A reboot is required after changing the property because bpfloader evaluates
- the kernel version while loading BPF programs during boot.

logic: for toggle

persist.sys.phh.traffic_indicator_fallback=true
    → uses the real kernel version
    → traffic statistics fallback enabled
    → recommended and default mode
    → firewall bypass may not work on some devices

persist.sys.phh.traffic_indicator_fallback=false
    → forces BPF version 5.10.239
    → disables the fallback
    → fully fixes firewall bypass
    → may break the traffic indicator
    → may cause black screen, OEM screen, Wi-Fi failure, or bootloader issues on incompatible kernels


Change-Id: Ie7e35ef29b8d343c180e892c9faf6501b497b94b
---
 loader/bpfloader.rs | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/loader/bpfloader.rs b/loader/bpfloader.rs
index a1ea554..ad114ad 100644
--- a/loader/bpfloader.rs
+++ b/loader/bpfloader.rs
@@ -426,8 +426,13 @@ fn parse_release(release: &str) -> (u32, u32, u32) {
 }
 
 fn kernel_version() -> Result<u32, anyhow::Error> {
-    if let Some(kver_override) = system_properties::read("ro.bpf.kver_override")? {
-        let (major, minor, sub) = parse_release(&kver_override);
+    let traffic_fallback = system_properties::read(
+        "persist.sys.phh.traffic_indicator_fallback",
+    )?
+    .unwrap_or_default();
+
+    if traffic_fallback == "false" {
+        let (major, minor, sub) = parse_release("5.10.239");
         return Ok(kver(major, minor, sub));
     }
     let mut buf: MaybeUninit<utsname> = MaybeUninit::zeroed();
